---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Stretch Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Stretch Easy - Guided Stretching Routines iOS app."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/stretch-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Stretch Easy?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Stretch%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What routines are included?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Stretch Easy comes with five pre-built routines: Morning Wake-Up (5 min), Desk Break (3 min), Post-Workout (10 min), Full Body (15 min), and Evening Wind-Down (7 min). Each targets different needs throughout your day.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I create my own routines?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes! The custom routine builder lets you pick from 15+ stretches, set custom durations for each, and save your routine for future use. Build routines tailored to your specific needs.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do the timers work?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Each stretch has a countdown timer with a large display. When time is up, you'll get a haptic cue (and optional audio) signaling it's time for the next stretch. Rest intervals between stretches give you time to transition.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does the Apple Watch app work independently?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes! The Apple Watch app includes all routines and can run completely on its own. Haptic feedback guides you through each stretch — no need to look at your phone.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What gets saved to HealthKit?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">If you enable HealthKit, completed stretching sessions are logged as flexibility workouts. This includes the routine name, duration, and calories (estimated). HealthKit integration is optional.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Is there a subscription?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">No. Stretch Easy is a one-time purchase with no subscriptions, no ads, and no in-app purchases. All features are included.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How often should I stretch?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Consistency matters more than duration. Even 3-5 minutes daily can improve flexibility over time. Use the Desk Break routine throughout the workday, or the Morning Wake-Up routine to start your day right.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I change the theme?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes! Stretch Easy includes 8 beautiful color themes. Go to Settings and choose the one that feels right for you.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
